# Provenance of rtl/snac_psx.v, which is copied from the repo below.
# rtl/sim/snac_psx/tb_snac_psx.sv is vendored alongside it from the same
# commit; the sha256 here covers the module only, since that is the file
# that gets synthesised.
#
# This module is NOT canonical here. It is copied from the AmigaCD USERSPACE
# repo, which owns it -- see rtl/README.md there, and the header of the module
# itself. Do not fix a bug in the copy: fix it there, then re-vendor, or the
# copies silently diverge and the next sync quietly reverts you.
#
# The repo/commit below named FringeCoder/Minimig-AGA-cd32-cdtv-native-akiko
# until 2026-09-15. That was the AmigaCD *core*, which carries a copy of this
# module, not its home: someone ran --stamp against a core checkout and the
# script writes whatever HEAD it is pointed at. The sha256 never changed, so
# nothing had drifted -- the pointer was simply to the wrong repository. It now
# names the commit in FringeCoder/AmigaCD whose blob hashes to the sha256 below.
#
# CI checks the local file against sha256 below. If that step fails, either the
# copy was edited in place (don't) or a re-vendor updated the file and not this
# stamp. Procedure: rtl/README.md in the FringeCoder/AmigaCD repo.
#
# Refresh with: ./snac_vendor_check.sh --stamp /path/to/amigacd-checkout

